{"name":"Sand Island","hex":"#f4d1c2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sand","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Rock that is ground more finely than gravel, but is not as fine as silt (more formally, see grain sizes chart), forming beaches and deserts and also used in construction.\n\n A specific grade, type, or composition of sand.\n\n A beach or other mass of sand.","A specific grade, type, or composition of sand."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a light beige colour, like that of typical sand."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sand"},{"term":"island","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A contiguous area of land, smaller than a continent, totally surrounded by water.","A contiguous area of land, smaller than a continent, partially surrounded by water; a peninsula; a half-island."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To surround with water; make into an island.","To set, dot (as if) with islands."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/island"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sand Island (Hawaii)","blocks":[{"text":"Sand Island, formerly known as Quarantine Island, is a small island within the city of Honolulu, Hawaii, United States. The island lies at the entrance to Honolulu Harbor."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/A_storm_is_coming_-_looking_over_Sand_Island_%2812576824565%29.jpg/330px-A_storm_is_coming_-_looking_over_Sand_Island_%2812576824565%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sand_Island_(Hawaii)","wikidata":"Q7415814"},{"title":"Sand island","blocks":[{"text":"A sand island is an island that is mostly made of sand."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Fraser_Island_a04_indian_head.jpg/330px-Fraser_Island_a04_indian_head.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sand_island","wikidata":"Q7415903"},{"title":"Sand","blocks":[{"text":"Sand is a granular material composed of finely divided mineral particles. Sand has various compositions but is usually defined by its grain size. Sand grains are smaller than gravel and coarser than silt. Sand can also refer to a textural class of soil or soil type; i.e., a soil containing more than 85 percent sand-sized particles by mass."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Libya_4608_Idehan_Ubari_Dunes_Luca_Galuzzi_2007.jpg/330px-Libya_4608_Idehan_Ubari_Dunes_Luca_Galuzzi_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sand","wikidata":"Q34679"},{"title":"Island","blocks":[{"text":"An island or isle is a piece of land, distinct from a continent, completely surrounded by water. There are continental islands, which were formed by being split from a continent by plate tectonics, and oceanic islands, which have never been part of a continent. Oceanic islands can be formed from volcanic activity, grow into atolls from coral reefs, and form from sediment along shorelines, creating barrier islands. River islands can also form from sediment and debris in rivers. Artificial islands are those made by humans, including small rocky outcroppings built out of lagoons and large-scale land reclamation projects used for development."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Hawaje-NoRedLine.jpg/330px-Hawaje-NoRedLine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Island","wikidata":"Q23442"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Cell_phone_tower_and_homes_as_seen_from_Sand_Island_in_Honolulu%2C_Oahu.jpg/500px-Cell_phone_tower_and_homes_as_seen_from_Sand_Island_in_Honolulu%2C_Oahu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Cell_phone_tower_and_homes_as_seen_from_Sand_Island_in_Honolulu%2C_Oahu.jpg/1280px-Cell_phone_tower_and_homes_as_seen_from_Sand_Island_in_Honolulu%2C_Oahu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Cell_phone_tower_and_homes_as_seen_from_Sand_Island_in_Honolulu%2C_Oahu.jpg/500px-Cell_phone_tower_and_homes_as_seen_from_Sand_Island_in_Honolulu%2C_Oahu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"View from Sand Island","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACell_phone_tower_and_homes_as_seen_from_Sand_Island_in_Honolulu%2C_Oahu.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Sand_Island_Beach%2C_Oahu%2C_Hawaii.jpg/500px-Sand_Island_Beach%2C_Oahu%2C_Hawaii.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Sand_Island_Beach%2C_Oahu%2C_Hawaii.jpg/1280px-Sand_Island_Beach%2C_Oahu%2C_Hawaii.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Sand_Island_Beach%2C_Oahu%2C_Hawaii.jpg/500px-Sand_Island_Beach%2C_Oahu%2C_Hawaii.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sand Island Beach","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASand_Island_Beach%2C_Oahu%2C_Hawaii.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/00065_sand_collage.jpg/500px-00065_sand_collage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/00065_sand_collage.jpg/1280px-00065_sand_collage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/00065_sand_collage.jpg/500px-00065_sand_collage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campai